The launch configuration used for .NET projects and file-based C# apps.

BuildConfiguration

• Name: BuildConfiguration                                                                                                                                               
• Modifiers: nullable get; set                                                                                                                                           
• Returns: string?                                                                                                                                                       
• Source: GitHub (https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/blob/b33d222049f1ecc3bc7257ec07b622fe550b2580/src/Aspire.Hosting/ApplicationModel/ExecutableLaunchConfiguration.cs)

Gets or sets the build configuration used to produce the project output.

public string? BuildConfiguration { get; set; }

Remarks

The value corresponds to the MSBuild Configuration property, such as Debug or Release.

BuildEnvironment

• Name: BuildEnvironment                                                                                                                                                 
• Modifiers: nullable get; set                                                                                                                                           
• Returns: Dictionary<string, string>                                                                                                                                    
• Source: GitHub (https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/blob/b33d222049f1ecc3bc7257ec07b622fe550b2580/src/Aspire.Hosting/ApplicationModel/ExecutableLaunchConfiguration.cs)

Gets or sets the resolved environment variables that affected the externally produced build.

public Dictionary<string, string>? BuildEnvironment { get; set; }

Remarks

IDE launchers use these authoritative values when evaluating build properties such as TargetPath. Empty means no project-specific build environment. These values are not a secret transport and can appear in build diagnostics.

BuildWorkingDirectory

• Name: BuildWorkingDirectory                                                                                                                                            
• Modifiers: nullable get; set                                                                                                                                           
• Returns: string?                                                                                                                                                       
• Source: GitHub (https://github.com/microsoft/aspire/blob/b33d222049f1ecc3bc7257ec07b622fe550b2580/src/Aspire.Hosting/ApplicationModel/ExecutableLaunchConfiguration.cs)

Gets or sets the working directory used by the externally produced build.

public string? BuildWorkingDirectory { get; set; }

Remarks

IDE launchers use this directory to select the same .NET SDK and repository configuration when evaluating project properties or rebuilding.

